methods.description:
Returns the verified participant for a Session this authority admitted: its role, outcome eligibility, Session lifetime and team. Returns [code]null[/code] for any other Session object, including a copy with the same ID.
[codeblock]
func _on_session_joined(session: SummerSession) -> void:
var participant := Summer.authority.match.get_participant(session)
if participant and participant.team >= 0:
spawn_on_side(session, participant.team)
[/codeblock]

SummerAuthorityRatings.description:
Lets the game own its rating rule. A queue declared in the build manifest with [code]"policy": "rating"[/code] and [code]"ratingSystemRef": "authority_v1"[/code] moves ratings only by the amounts the authority reports: read each player's rating, compare it with what the players achieved, and pass every player's movement to [method SummerAuthorityMatch.conclude]. Matchmaking then groups players by the moved ratings. Ratings read here are for the authority's own game logic: never show one player's rating to other players. [method leaderboard] is the public view.
[codeblock]
# A co-op run: every player cleared a dungeon rated 1450.
var deltas: Dictionary[SummerSession, int] = {}
for session in sessions:
var read := Summer.authority.ratings.load(session)
await read.get_result_or_completed_signal()
var expected := 1.0 / (1.0 + pow(10.0, (1450 - read.rating.value) / 400.0))
deltas[session] = roundi(32 * ((1.0 if timed else 0.0) - expected))
var outcomes: Dictionary[SummerSession, SummerAuthorityMatch.MatchOutcome] = {}
for session in sessions:
outcomes[session] = SummerAuthorityMatch.MATCH_OUTCOME_WIN if timed else SummerAuthorityMatch.MATCH_OUTCOME_LOSS
await Summer.authority.match.conclude(outcomes, "dungeon_complete", deltas).get_result_or_completed_signal()
[/codeblock]

methods.description:
The one way into a World. The [param target] names the placement provider (matchmaking queue, direct World, invite, follow, portal, resume, or local fixture); every provider returns the same [SummerJoinOperation] with the same progress, typed failures, [member SummerJoinOperation.world] and [member SummerJoinOperation.session]. Only a queue target can emit [signal SummerJoinOperation.acceptance_required].
After a hosted connection is lost, a new queue or World join first awaits confirmed removal of the previous Session, then starts the requested placement within the original join deadline. Canceling that pending join stops the new placement but does not undo the durable Session cleanup.
[codeblock]
var op := Summer.client.join(SummerJoinTarget.world(world_id))
var joined: SummerResult = await op.get_result_or_completed_signal()
if joined.ok:
    enter_gameplay_with(op.world, op.session)
[/codeblock]
A provider this runtime cannot reach yet fails typed with [code]unsupported_placement[/code].

SummerClientFriends.description:
With the player's consent, this view lists the player's Summer friends and whether each is offline, online, or playing this Game. A Game never learns which other Game a friend is playing. The trusted Summer app owns friendship, friend requests, blocking and chat; [method show_friends], [method show_profile] and [method show_chat] ask the app to present those screens over the game, and need no consent.
Reading friends needs the [code]social.friends.read[/code] permission: the Build declares it, and the player grants it in the Summer app's consent sheet, which [method request_access] asks the app to show. [method get_access] reports the player's current decision. The Engine re-reads the friends when they change, when the event stream starts or resyncs, after a consent decision, on [method refresh], and about every 60 seconds while a handler is connected to [signal changed] and the game is in front; friend status changes are not pushed. Every signal is emitted after the view is updated, once per change.
[codeblock]
var friends := Summer.client.friends
friends.changed.connect(_show_friends)

func _on_friends_button_pressed() -> void:
    if not friends.is_available():
        return
    if friends.get_access() != &"granted":
        var decision: SummerResult = await friends.request_access().completed
        if not decision.is_ok():
            return # The player kept their friends private.
    _show_friends()

func _show_friends() -> void:
    for friend in friends.get_friends():
        add_row(friend.display_name, friend.status == &"in_this_game")
[/codeblock]

SummerClientMessages.description:
Reads and sends the player's direct messages with their friends: the same account history the Summer app shows. Each operation needs its own permission, which the Build declares and the player grants in the Summer app's consent sheet: [code]social.messages.read[/code] for [method list_conversations], [method list_messages] and [method list_messages_after]; [code]social.messages.send[/code] for [method send]; and [code]social.messages.read_state.write[/code] for [method mark_read]. Friendship, blocks and the age rule still apply to every message.
Message text is plain Unicode, never markup, and passes the Summer chat text filter. Names and message text that reach the game never carry control characters other than newline and tab in message text; a read that would deliver one fails with [code]protocol_error[/code] and changes nothing. Without a permission an operation fails with [code]permission_not_requested[/code], [code]permission_declined[/code], [code]permission_revoked[/code] or [code]permission_undeclared[/code], matching [method get_access]; ask with [method request_access]. Other typed failures are [code]text_not_allowed[/code] (the filter refused the text; nothing was stored), [code]target_unavailable[/code] (the other player is not a friend, blocked this player, or is gone), [code]rate_limited[/code] (retryable), [code]age_restricted[/code], [code]invalid_argument[/code], [code]capability_unavailable[/code] when [method is_available] is [code]false[/code], and [code]unavailable[/code] (retryable) when the Player Host cannot be reached.
[codeblock]
var messages := Summer.client.messages
messages.messages_changed.connect(_reload_thread)

func _send(friend_id: String, text: String) -> void:
    var op := messages.send(friend_id, text)
    var result: SummerResult = await op.completed
    if result.code == &"permission_not_requested":
        if (await messages.request_access([&"social.messages.send"]).completed).is_ok():
            op = messages.send(friend_id, text)
            result = await op.completed
    if result.is_ok():
        add_bubble(op.message)
[/codeblock]

SummerClientParty.description:
A Summer party belongs to the player's account and follows them across Games. This view shows its members, its leader, which members have this Game open, data this Game shares with the party, and whether the party is searching a queue in this Game. The trusted Summer app owns creating parties, invitations, kicking, leadership transfer and chat; [method show_invite_dialog] and [method show_party_dialog] ask the app to present those screens. The Game never sees the party ID, invitations, chat, another Game's data, or which other Game a member is playing.
The view is a snapshot read through the Player Host whenever the party changes, when the event stream starts or resyncs, and on [method refresh]. Every signal is emitted after the snapshot is updated, once per real change. Getters return empty values outside a party and when [method is_available] is [code]false[/code]: in local play, for a guest, or when the Summer app does not offer parties.
To bring the party into a match, the leader joins [method SummerJoinTarget.party_queue]; every other member follows by joining the same target when [signal search_started] fires.
[codeblock]
var party := Summer.client.party
party.search_started.connect(func(queue: StringName) -> void:
    if not party.is_leader():
        var result := await Summer.client.join(SummerJoinTarget.party_queue(queue)).completed
        if not result.is_ok():
            push_warning(result.message)
)

func _on_play_pressed(queue: StringName) -> void:
    if party.is_in_party():
        if party.is_leader():
            await Summer.client.join(SummerJoinTarget.party_queue(queue)).completed
    else:
        await Summer.client.join(SummerJoinTarget.queue(queue)).completed
[/codeblock]
Games typically disable Play for members, show each member's [member SummerPartyMember.in_game], and use [method set_data] so members see the leader's selection.

SummerStandingOperation.description:
Completes with the caller's rating, how many players are rated in the queue, their percentile once rated, and their leaderboard rank when it is within the top 1000. Players are ordered exactly as on the leaderboard. The members are empty until the operation succeeds.
[codeblock]
var standing := Summer.client.ratings.standing(&"dungeon")
await standing.get_result_or_completed_signal()
if standing.rank > 0:
label.text = "#%d of %d" % [standing.rank, standing.players]
elif standing.rated:
label.text = "Top %.1f%%" % (100.0 - standing.percentile)
[/codeblock]
